# How a function is compiled does not hang on who calls it in a loop: a test would never run the code that ships. The twin, field-left-out-is-read-alike-in-a-function-that-a-loop-calls.ir, is this program and two lines more,
# and the check lines on the two readers are the same in both files. The file is checked, so somebody has written what the receiver is: the object itself is asked what has become of it, and behind its answer an empty slot is undefined.
# f1 = isFragile, f2 = hasNoLabel
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetSlotOrUndefined v0 {{*}}key="fragile" {{*}}level=Expected
# CHECK: = StrictEq
# RUN(ALONE): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# ALONE-NOT: = PropGet
# ALONE-NOT: = ShapeTest
# RUN(NAME): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# NAME-LABEL: code f2:Body
# NAME: = ShapeTest v0
# NAME: = HasNoExtraProperties
# NAME: = PropGet v0 key="label"
# NAME: = HasLayoutPrototype
# NAME: = AreMembersUnchanged
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: true false true true
